      "angle": "The bargain is structurally asymmetric: the immunity is immediate, categorical, and permanent; the compensation is deferred, tabulated, and capped. Every federal injury-compensation-for-immunity swap in the record has delivered the shield in full and the remedy in part.",
      "why": "This is the skeptic's core competence — reading a governance proposal as an allocation of power rather than as a design diagram. It does not require denying that the no-fault board could help some claimants; it only requires showing that the two halves of the trade are not enforced with equal reliability. It also lets Skeptic attack without appearing anti-compensation, which is the trap the affirmative is setting.",
