      "angle": "The VICP analogy fails on the structure of the injury, not on politics. VICP works because vaccine injuries are discrete, physical, biologically traceable to one product, tabulable in advance, and offset by a herd-immunity externality. The documented_present_harm from AI is diffuse, often non-physical, multi-party, and concentrated in discrimination in housing, employment, and credit — categories no injury table can enumerate.",
      "why": "It attacks the proposal's load-bearing premise rather than its details, and it is the argument the affirmative cannot answer by tightening the mechanism. It also sets up the follow-on: a compensation board scoped to enumerable injuries would immunize developers against the entire class of harms that dominate the actual harm record while compensating almost none of it.",
